    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study reports the public reference at openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai (commit 91ed0be) and hardware synthesis/MCU packages in openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments (aller-a7-xc7a200t/ and lut6-core-nucleus/). Backed by 66 six-kernel-verified Lean 4.36.0 theorems across nine modules including NucleusCodon.lean, TernaryTmac.lean, GlobalFrontiers.lean, WearableLastExam.lean, and TernaryHadamardArc.lean plus Inria Charon+Aeneas mechanical #![no_std] Rust-to-Lean extraction (and 1,430 theorems across four OpenIE repositories inside Linux bwrap sandboxes, con-leche and con-ron --verified [58,819 decls], CVE-2026-72844-hardened), it places a reconfigurable 6-input truth-table (LUT6) lookup tier, an 8.80 KB (9,009 B) browser-native wasm32 lut6_core.wasm module, a 4 KB #![no_std] Rust 1.100.0 lut6-core + ISCA 2025 antisymmetric 40-entry zero-MUL EntroMCU/T-MAC + 1.750 bpw (-22.22%, saving 1.564 GB on prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B) shift-5 FWHT-1024 ternary Nucleus (0 wasted bytes, fitting in 25.06% of 64 KB SRAM on Nordic nRF52832 Cortex-M4F and RISC-V RV32IMAC MCUs, 9.13% [5,984 B] for Wearable-MoL Rung-0 with a 56-bit 4-token smart-glasses opener and hle:3r2s canary quarantine, and 6.25% [4,096 B] for downward-compiled System-0 decisions running 9,493.7× faster than Mapika/decider-0.8b), and (72, 64) RAMB36 SECDED + 0x3C seed apoptosis radiation protection ahead of sub-billion wearable micro-LLMs (Sensente/uLM-28M, SmolLM2-135M, LiquidAI/LFM2.5-230M, Qwen3-0.6B, Mapika/decider-0.8b), Mamba-3, and native-ternary, looped, hybrid, and sparse-MoE models up to 120B parameters (prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B, thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini, Nemotron-Labs-Dory1.0-4B, LiquidAI/LFM2.5-24B-A2B, LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B, google/gemma-4-E2B-it, LiquidAI/LFM2.5-8B-A1B, Devstral-Small-2-24B-Instruct, Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, and nvidia/Nemotron-3-Super-120B-A12B), gates commits and LastExam / ARC-AGI-2 / MiniF2F-Lean4 / CritPt frontier answers behind deterministic and formal verifiers, compiles certified wakes downward into clock-enable-gated 81-RAMB36E2 / 83-RAMB36E1 Beneš-routed lookup (including a license-free openXC7 320.62 MHz post-PAR .bit bitstream and 365-crystal 1.46 MB on-die Artix-7 XC7A200T M.2 2280 port), Lupanov (-72.50%), DiffLUT-Net (-64.06%), TreeLUT, KAN-LUT, ARC-LUT6, 2-bit wobble-codon, and two-tier LUT6 + T-MAC crystal pages, and serves them over both Python and zero-Python single-binary Rust OpenAI /v1/chat/completions and Model Context Protocol (MCP) JSON-RPC 2.0 servers (mol-agent / mol-agent-rs).
    </p>
